    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_data_title">Data handling</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_body">CoreAlert processes call and contact data on your device. If you enable VIP message alerts, notification metadata is processed locally to identify paired direct conversations; message text, contact names and phone numbers from notifications are never stored. Only hashed conversation identifiers and technical deduplication fingerprints are saved.\n\nCall monitoring runs entirely on your phone: it never uploads your contacts, call history or location, and nothing is sent to a server.\n\nA backup you export is a local file encrypted with a password you choose; CoreAlert never sees that password.\n\nCoreAlert does not protect against a compromised phone, malware, screenshots, or keyloggers.\n\nNo analytics, no tracking, no ads.\n\n100% offline — no Firebase, no analytics SDKs, no advertising, no third-party scripts and no push notifications. Nothing you enter ever leaves your phone: the production build opens no network connection at all.</string>
